          "en": "1. Granting or refusing to grant an Enterprise Registration Certificate, or requiring the founder of an enterprise to submit additional documents contrary to the provisions of this Law; causing delay, nuisance, obstruction or harassment to the founder of an enterprise and to the business activities of the enterprise.\n2. Obstructing the owner, member or shareholder of an enterprise from performing the rights and obligations in accordance with this Law and the company charter.\n3. Conducting business in the form of an enterprise without registration, or continuing to do business after the Enterprise Registration Certificate has been revoked or while the enterprise's business activities are suspended.\n4. Declaring untruthfully or inaccurately the contents of the business registration file and the contents of the file for registration of changes to business registration contents.\n5. Declaring charter capital falsely, failing to contribute in full the charter capital as registered; intentionally valuing contributed assets incorrectly.\n6. Doing business in lines of business prohibited from investment and business; doing business in lines of business to which market access has not been opened for foreign investors; doing business in conditional lines of business without satisfying the business conditions in accordance with law or without ensuring the maintenance of sufficient conditions for investment and business during operation.\n7. Fraud, money laundering and terrorism financing."
