          "en": "1. The provincial-level business registration office shall issue a decision cancelling the decision revoking the enterprise registration certificate and shall concurrently restore the enterprise registration certificate on the national information system on enterprise registration in the following cases:\na) The provincial-level business registration office determines that the enterprise does not fall within the cases of revocation of the enterprise registration certificate;\nb) The provincial-level business registration office receives a document of the tax administration agency requesting the restoration of the legal status of the enterprise after the enterprise has had its enterprise registration certificate revoked at the request of the tax administration agency.\n2. The provincial-level business registration office shall issue a decision cancelling the revocation decision and restoring the enterprise registration certificate, and shall concurrently update the legal status of the enterprise, branches, representative offices and business locations in the national database on enterprise registration within 03 working days from the date of determining that the enterprise does not fall within the cases of revocation of the enterprise registration certificate, or from the date of receipt of the request document of the tax administration agency. The provincial-level business registration office shall be responsible before the law for the decision cancelling the decision revoking the enterprise registration certificate and for the restoration of the enterprise registration certificate on the national information system on enterprise registration.\n3. Within 03 working days from the date of issuance of the decision cancelling the decision revoking the enterprise registration certificate, the provincial-level business registration office shall send the decision to the head office of the enterprise, send a notice on the restoration of the enterprise registration certificate to the tax administration agency, and post the notice and the decision on the national business registration portal."
